data.db filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# This module's Go sources are LF in the index and must be LF in the worktree
# too. gofmt compares the bytes ON DISK, so a CRLF checkout makes `gofmt -l`
# list a file that is byte-identical to a clean one. Measured on
# pubvera-trialvera's providers.go: gofmt listed it, the file had CRLF endings,
# and CI on Linux passed green — a false positive that costs a diagnosis every
# time it fires. eol=lf overrides core.autocrlf=true, which put the CRLF there.
*.go text eol=lf